          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Why is area generally measured using squares?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.197,
            0.514,
            0.286
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Draw a circle on a graph sheet with diameter (breadth) of length 3. Count the squares and use them to estimate the area of the circular region."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.29,
            0.488,
            0.447
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "As you can see, circles can’t be packed tightly without gaps in between. So, it is difficult to get an accurate measurement of area using circles as units. Here, the same rectangle is packed in two different ways with circles — the"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
