        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.484,
            0.834,
            0.596
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Try using different shapes (triangle and rectangle) to fill the given space (without overlaps and gaps) and find out the merits associated with using a square shape to find the area rather than another shape. List out the points that make a square the best shape to use to measure area."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.158,
            0.6,
            0.833,
            0.642
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1. Find the area (in square metres) of the floor outside of the corridor."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.158,
            0.648,
            0.833,
            0.692
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2. Find the area (in square metres) occupied by your school playground."
